<title>USA: Coke to record $320 million non-cash benefit.</title>
<headline>Coke to record $320 million non-cash benefit.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Coca-Cola Co. said Friday it would record a $320 million one-time gain in the third quarter after reaching an agreement in principle with the Internal Revenue Service on a number of issues dating back to 1981.</p>
<p>Coke said the accounting benefit arose because, under the agreement, accruals that had been recorded for taxes would be reduced.</p>
<p>It said the agreement ended negotiations it has had with the IRS over issues including litigation involving its operations in Puerto Rico.</p>
<p>Coke's stock fell 75 cents to $50.875 in afternoon trading on the New York Stock Exchange.</p>
